WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.160
- I always enjoy sharing cool stories

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.010
from social media that
might make you smile.

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.331
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.331 --> 00:00:08.600
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.320
So giving birth under the best
of circumstances is no joke.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.580
It's no fun.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.020
So imagine going into labor

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.000
and not being able to
get to any medical care.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.550
It happened to a mama in rural Virginia

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.170
just after a monster
snowstorm came through.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.850
The power lines were knocked down.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.930
Trees blocked all the roads

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.170
and more than a foot of snow
had amassed on the ground,

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.080
but she didn't let any
of that stand in the way

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.480
of getting to the hospital,

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.930
trekking a quarter mile through the snow

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.319
to get to an ambulance.

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:38.152
(audience groans)

00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:39.840
You know she wanted that baby out.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.610
She was like, get out.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.930
We have that brave mama
on the line right now

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.510
along with her husband and baby girl.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.800
Let's say hi to Noel,
Chris and baby Josephine

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.253
watching on NBC Washington.

00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:53.880
Hi.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.240
Oh my gosh, you are adorable.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.470
Look at baby Josephine.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.973
Hi, hello.

00:01:00.878 --> 00:01:02.860
(laughs)

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.490
Well congrats on baby Josephine.

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:07.640
So the snowstorm was worse
than you expected, right?

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.890
- It was way worse.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.200
We knew it was supposed to snow

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.330
but it had been like 60
degrees the night before,

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.500
so we weren't expecting it to be that bad.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.810
But when we woke up, there
was like a foot of snow

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.860
on the ground and it was still falling.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.520
And then trees started coming down.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.010
We lost power.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.680
And Noel was over a week overdue

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.740
with our fourth child.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.340
So I went out to see if we could even

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.290
get to the road from our dead end street.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.850
And I saw like a barricade
of about 30 or 40 trees

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.500
all meshed together with power lines.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.333
I tried to get through

00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:38.320
and ended up stepping on a power line.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.210
So I came back to the
house and I said to Noel,

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.150
you can't go into labor.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.010
Don't move.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.390
Just sit down because
we can't get out of here

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.833
and nobody is coming to us.
- So what did you do?

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.000
You're treking to the,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.940
are you just like,

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.320
what is your emotional state

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.510
while you're trekking to an ambulance?

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:54.820
I mean, are you at the
point where you're kind

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.300
of anger or laughing hysterically?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.523
'Cause you're like ha ha ha ha ha, like-

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.260
- Going in between the two.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.430
- Oh my gosh.
- Oh my gosh, Kelly,

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.160
I was seriously panicking, like really.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.030
So I wake up in labor and then,

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.960
you know, we tried to call my mom

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.550
and anyone else we could think of

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.720
that could possibly get to us

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.380
so we could go to the hospital.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.800
No one could get out.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.230
We called 911, silence.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.270
We couldn't get through.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.960
Luckily my mom was able to get ahold of

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.890
the fire and rescue up by her

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.610
who then called Stafford Fire and Rescue

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.710
and they were able to get to me.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.600
But Kelly, they had to
walk a mile through snow

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.810
and fallen down trees to get to me.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.360
And by the time they got here,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.330
I had my boots on, I had my
bag packed, I was ready to go

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.580
and they sat me down and
they said, absolutely not.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.050
We cannot leave.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.070
But then I thought,

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.760
okay well there's a parallel street

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.180
that runs in our backyard,
like across the way.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.230
If the ambulance can get there,

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.930
maybe we can walk to
the ambulance that way.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.690
So we went ahead and tried.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.845
My contractions were about two
minutes apart at this point.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:03.800
So we had to stop every
time I had a contraction

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.940
but we walked through fallen down trees

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.740
and frozen creeks and chicken wire.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.890
And we'd already decided
that we were gonna

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.050
name the baby after St. Joseph

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.060
and it really felt like, you know,

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.745
the Mary and Joseph, you
know, trek to Bethlehem.

00:03:18.745 --> 00:03:20.380
(laughs)

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.400
And finally we get to the ambulance

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.800
and then baby Josephine was
born 7:00 AM the next morning.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.340
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.640
Well I'm just telling you what,

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.140
baby Josephine, she's supposed
to do something powerful,

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.260
something wonderful with her life.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.086
Thank you so much Noel and
Chris for sharing your story.

00:03:39.086 --> 00:03:39.919
- [Noel] Thank you Kelly.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.154
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:41.987
(ding)

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:43.010
That's not all though.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.617
Our season long partner,
Pilot pen, makers of FriXion,

00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:48.250
the to go erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.970
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly just like y'all.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.100
I mean, you are fearless ma'am.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.737
So they are giving you a
thousand dollars just to say

00:03:55.737 --> 00:03:56.886
you're awesome.

00:03:56.886 --> 00:03:58.210
- Oh whoa.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.345
Thank you.

00:03:59.345 --> 00:04:01.430
It's all going to coffee and diapers.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.720
- Oh my God, right?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.553
Yeah.

00:04:03.553 --> 00:04:04.386
It is expensive.

00:04:04.386 --> 00:04:05.370
Babies are expensive.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.203
You are right.

00:04:06.203 --> 00:04:07.240
Well God bless y'all.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.153
Enjoy those four beautiful children.

